  "notes": "Boot a Red and Ted's Road Show ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, open the WPC Security service menu, step to T.17 \"TED\" TEST and start it. The test runs by itself and names each step on the display: 01 EYES WIDE, 02 EYES LEFT, 03 EYES RIGHT, 04 EYES CLOSED, 05 EYES OPEN, 06 MOUTH OPEN, 07 MOUTH CLOSED and 08 RUN MOUTH, then repeats. Frames 0.5 s apart cover the eye steps; two output checkpoints wait for public 19 on two successive cycles, each followed by frames 0.4 s apart through the mouth steps, so a missed menu edge fails the run.",
